<title>JAPAN: Nippon Mining cuts copper price by 10,000 yen.</title>
<headline>Nippon Mining cuts copper price by 10,000 yen.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nippon Mining and Metals Co said on Monday it had cut its selling price for electrolytic copper by 10,000 yen to 340,000 yen per tonne, effective immediately.</p>
<p>Major Japanese smelters periodically review their selling prices, changing them in line with market prices and currency rates.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7431</p>
</text>
